# DS2103: one warning per `sort`; the fix adds `asc` to every key without a direction,
# including a key with `nulls last` and a long expression.
mode: check
schema: t(x: long, y: real, s: string, ts: datetime, b: bool)
---- query
from t | sort by x, y desc, s nulls last, strlen(strcat(s, "-", s, "-", s, "-", s, "-", s))
---- expected
warning[DS2103]: `sort` key without `asc` or `desc`
  --> query:1:18
  |
1 | from t | sort by x, y desc, s nulls last, strlen(strcat(s, "-", s, "-", s, "-", s, "-", s))
  |                  ^          -             ------------------------------------------------- this key has no direction either
  |                  |          |
  |                  |          this key has no direction either
  |                  |
  |                  sorted ascending, while KQL sorts descending by default
  |
  = help: write the direction: `x asc`, or `x desc` for largest first
